  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Equation of tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Solving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Another point of intersection is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>So, now plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0055_95e78b1a38d6.png\" style=\"width: 314px; height: 237px;\" /></p><p>Required area from the above diagram will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence this is the required option.</p>"
